{"format":1,"seq":193,"writes":[{"type":"entry","value":{"model":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So the root cause is clear: the program declared body as a string, but the model sent a JSON-encoded string literal with extra quotes, and since a string input admits that, it passed through unchanged. The fix is for pit to detect when the string is actually a JSON string literal and decode it, though there's an edge case risk if a legitimate string happens to look like quoted JSON.\n\nI don't have push access to cv/pit, so I'm weighing whether I can even file an issue there versus just preparing a patch and testing it locally against pit's codebase to produce a ready-to-use diff. Let me check the tests for resolveToolInput to understand expected behavior.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_bdrk_01S54uuv2kFn3pVpowwB9SzB","name":"typescript","arguments":{"code":"// @pit: {\"label\": \"Find pit tests for resolveToolInput\"}\nasync ({ shell: { exec } }) => {\n  const r = await exec(`cd /tmp/pit && grep -rln \"resolveToolInput\" . --include=*.ts | grep -v node_modules; grep -rn -A3 \"resolveToolInput(\" test | head -40`, {});\n  return r.stdout;\n}"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"nvidia","model":"aws/anthropic/bedrock-claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":670,"cacheRead":27289,"cacheWrite":1187,"totalTokens":29148,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":false},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":490},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794611770160,"responseId":"msg_bdrk_u2n7cosdoliw76eyejiwr7pqrctc4ry2bjbzjyga3xmfubowpgma","rawStopReason":"tool_use","durationMs":9499,"thinkingLevel":"medium"}],"kind":"pi.assistant","id":83,"conversationId":1,"byTaskId":82}},{"type":"task","value":{"id":82,"conversationId":1,"kind":"pi.generation","version":2,"input":{},"background":false,"abortRequested":false,"state":{"status":"waiting","checkpoint":{"phase":"tools","assistant